        <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="f-1269_lbl" order="0" xlink:to="ft-1269_47434_lbl" />
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-89_46946_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"><b style="font-weight: bold; font-style: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)">Schedule Page 700 Line No.: 12 Column: c</b></span></span></span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><br /></span></span></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-decoration: inherit">Enable Bakken has no trunk lines, and, accordingly, has no barrel-mile data to report.</span></span></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Roboto"><br /></span></span></span><br /></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-282_47082_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none">Cash management program with Energy Transfer LP.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-634_47254_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b style="font-weight: bold">Schedule Page 114 Line No.: 1 Column: c</b></span></span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">In accordance with the Order Denying Rehearing, Denying Petition and Granting Remedies in Docket No. RM20-14-004 issued on November 20, 2025 footnote 111, we have determined that rebillings, as permitted in that Order, are not distortive. Accordingly, rebillings in the amount of $0.5 million are included in Account(s) 600.</span></span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><br /></span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-661_47029_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p style="text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(51, 51, 51, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); float: none; display: inline !important">Cash management program with Energy Transfer LP.</span><br /></p></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-733_47036_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>Schedule Page 212 Line No.: 47 Column: g</b></span></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">On July 1, 2025, Bighorn Devco LLC, an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer, merged into Enable Bakken. As the surviving entity, Enable Bakken acquired all of Bighorns rights, titles, and interests. This transaction included the transfer of $26 million in carrier property.</span></span> </span><br /></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-905_47037_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>Schedule Page 216 Line No.: 43 Column: e</b></span></span></p><p><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">On July 1, 2025, Bighorn Devco LLC, an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer, merged into Enable Bakken. As the surviving entity, Enable Bakken acquired all of Bighorn's rights, titles, and interests. This transaction included the transfer of $9,309,436 in carrier property's accumulated depreciation.<br /></span></span><br /></p></div></link:footnote>
        <link:footnote xlink:label="ft-1269_47434_lbl" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en-US" xlink:type="resource" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><div><p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><b style="font-weight: bold; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-style: normal; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)">Schedule Page 700 Line No.: 9 Column: b</b></span></span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; background-color: unset; text-align: inherit">In accordance with the Order Denying Rehearing, Denying Petition and Granting Remedies in Docket No. RM20-14-004 issued on November 20, 2025 footnote 111, we have determined that rebillings, as permitted in that Order, are not distortive. Accordingly, rebillings in the amount of $502,078 are included in line 10, interstate operating revenue. These revenues represent a one-time event and are not representative of future revenues. </span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Roboto"><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><br /></span></span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none">The cost of service results were calculated using the Cost of Service Model. This model calculates cost of service using the Trended Original Cost methodology promulgated by the FERC in Opinion No. 154-B, 31 FERC 61,377 (1985), as modified and clarified by subsequent rulings.</span></p><p style="margin: 0; color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); text-align: left"><span style="color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: left; text-indent: 0; white-space: normal; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); display: inline !important; float: none"><br /></span><span style="font-size: 12pt"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><br /></span></span></p></div></link:footnote>
    </link:footnoteLink>
</xbrl>